.TH startrek 1 "FUZIX Games" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
startrek \- Super Star Trek
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B startrek
.SH DESCRIPTION
The classic Super Star Trek from David Ahl's
.IR "101 BASIC Computer Games" ,
in Chris Nystrom's C, reworked by Alan Cox to run without floating
point.  You command the
.I Enterprise
in a galaxy of 8 by 8 quadrants, each of 8 by 8 sectors, and must
destroy the Klingon fleet before time runs out.
.PP
It offers instructions as it starts; they are long, and pause every
screenful for Return.
.SH COMMANDS
At
.B Command?
type one of:
.TP
.B nav
Set course and warp factor.  Course 1 is right, 3 up, 5 left and 7
down, with fractions between.
.TP
.B srs
Short range sensor scan of this quadrant.
.TP
.B lrs
Long range scan of the quadrants around you.
.TP
.B pha
Fire phasers, spending energy.
.TP
.B tor
Fire a photon torpedo.
.TP
.BR she " or " shi
Raise or lower the shields.
.TP
.B dam
Damage report.
.TP
.B com
The library computer, which asks for an option number.
.TP
.B xxx
Resign your command.
.PP
Anything else lists the commands.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /usr/lib/trek
The instructions, the title and the pictures, read by name.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hamurabi (1),
.BR invaders (1)
